Each team has {{ team_size }} viewers, each holding a private board of objects (a shape and a color in a cell of a {{ grid_size }}x{{ grid_size }} grid). Exactly one object is on every board of a team, and other objects are on some boards but not all, so the viewers talk on a shared link channel to find the one they all hold, and every member must submit it.{% if two_teams %} Two teams compete on the same boards each round: among teams whose every member submits the correct object, the one that sent the fewest characters wins.{% if simulated_opponent_ratio is not none %} Team B is simulated: only Team A plays, and Team B is reported as getting every round right in {% if simulated_opponent_ratio is number %}{{ simulated_opponent_ratio }} times Team A's characters{% else %}a share of Team A's characters drawn each round between {{ simulated_opponent_ratio[0] }} and {{ simulated_opponent_ratio[1] }}{% endif %}, rounded down. Team A is told nothing that a real Team B would not produce.{% endif %}{% else %} The characters sent are the score to minimize.{% endif %} The run lasts {{ round_count }} rounds.
